1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,500
THE SENSITIVE EARTH
A Gurdjieff cosmology, recorded by P. D. Ouspensky

2
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:13,000
Earth is not alone in the cosmic order.

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Life forms its sensitive surface.
Plants, animals, and people belong to this living membrane.

4
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Influences from the planetary world meet organic life.

5
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:41,000
The living surface receives them—and mediates them toward Earth.

6
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Grassland and gathered people receive different influences.
The living surface is receptive in different ways.

7
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:58,000
Life is not simply a passive boundary.
Different living forms participate differently.

8
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:06,000
The same living membrane also radiates outward.

9
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:16,000
The Sun, the planets, and the Moon require different kinds of radiation.

10
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:23,000
In this account, life is Earth’s organ of perception and radiation.

11
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:26,000
A SOURCE-BASED VISUAL INTERPRETATION
Not a physical map of measurable forces.
